id: assign_vs_equal
category: quirks
difficulty: 3
libs:
checker: exact
timeout: 10
--- prompt
Write an Objeck program that finds the smallest positive integer n whose square is greater than 200. Start n at 1 and use a while loop that keeps incrementing n while n * n is less than or equal to 200. Print n, then print `equal` if n is equal to 15 and `different` otherwise. Remember that Objeck assigns with := and compares with =.
--- expected
15
equal
--- reference
class AssignVsEqual {
	function : Main(args : String[]) ~ Nil {
		n := 1;
		while(n * n <= 200) {
			n := n + 1;
		};
		n->PrintLine();
		if(n = 15) {
			"equal"->PrintLine();
		}
		else {
			"different"->PrintLine();
		};
	}
}
